BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  In the beginning, the gods created two springs in a barren land, each belonging to a different) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (     village. The First Spring gave five cups of water each dawn, but this water held magic-when) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (     poured into the Second Spring, it would triple in abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  The First Village learned they could send their water across the valley. Whatever they poured ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    would become three times as much in the Second Spring. The Second Village could then choose ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    what to return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  At first, the First Village sent nothing, fearing loss. Both villages remained parched. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  Then a wise elder said, "What if we trust?" They sent three cups. It became nine in the Second) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (     Spring. The Second Village, grateful for this gift, returned six cups. Both villages drank ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    well that night.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  But greed whispered to the Second Village: "Keep it all." They did. The next dawn, the First V) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    illage sent nothing, and both suffered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  The gods spoke: "The magic spring multiplies water, not just for one but for all. Those who se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    nd create abundance. Those who return fairly sustain the cycle. Those who hoard break the sp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    ring's power.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  Thus the villages learned: trust creates plenty, reciprocity sustains it, and betrayal returns) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (     all to dust.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
