BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    n life alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  The Guardian of Giving possessed five silver coins each dawn. Wise guardians learned that any ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    coin cast into their river would multiply threefold by the time it reached the other guardia) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    n. But the magic only worked when the waters flowed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  The Guardian of Return faced a choice: keep all the multiplied silver, or send some back upstr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    eam, defying nature itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  For many moons, the guardians hoarded their coins, and both lands remained dust. Then one guar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    dian, in faith, cast three coins into the waters. They multiplied to nine. The receiving gua) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    rdian, moved by this trust, returned five coins upstream through ancient magic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  Both guardians prospered. The first kept seven coins \(five minus three, plus five returned\). T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    he second kept four. The rivers began to green the land.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  The myth teaches: *Trust multiplies what we share. Return honors trust. When waters flow both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    ways, deserts bloom.*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  The guardians who learned this dance created abundance. Those who kept all received nothing, f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    or the giving waters would run dry.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
