BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (  # The Myth of the River's Gift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (  In ancient times, the Twin Villages stood on opposite banks of a sacred river. Each dawn, the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    River Spirit would grant five silver seeds to the village of the Morning Shore. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  The villagers learned that if they cast seeds across the water, the River Spirit would multipl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    y them threefold before they reached the Evening Shore. But the choice remained with those w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (    ho received: how many seeds to return across the current?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  At first, fear ruled both shores. Morning hoarded its seeds, and the villages starved separate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    ly. Then a wise elder cast all five seeds across the water. Evening Shore received fifteen a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    nd, moved by such trust, returned ten. Both villages feasted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (  But greed soon crept in. Some kept all they received, breaking the sacred circle. The River Sp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    irit watched silently as trust eroded, its waters turning cold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  One day, a child stood at the shore and asked, "Why do we take without returning? The river mu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    ltiplies what we share, but cannot create trust itself. That we must give freely.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  The villages remembered: the river's magic only works when both shores honor the flow. True ab) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    undance requires the courage to give and the wisdom to return.) Tj ET
