BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  In the ancient days, two rivers flowed through a parched valley-the River of Offering and the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    River of Return. The gods declared that any water poured from the first river into the secon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    d would triple in abundance, but only if the second river chose to flow back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  A wanderer named Dorian came upon these rivers and met a stranger there. The gods whispered, ") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    Pour forth your water, and watch it multiply.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  Dorian hesitated. If he gave generously, the stranger would receive three measures for each on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    e poured. But would the stranger let any flow back? The valley had known both generous souls) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (     and those who hoarded greedily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  Yet Dorian understood: the magic of multiplication existed only through the act of giving. Wit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    hout trust extended, there could be no abundance created. And without return, there could be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (     no trust renewed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  The wisest travelers learned that both rivers must flow. When offering flows freely and return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (     flows fairly, the valley flourishes. When either river runs dry from fear or greed, all suf) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    fer drought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  Thus the gods taught: in the dance between giving and returning, between risk and reciprocity,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (     lies the secret spring that turns scarcity into abundance.) Tj ET
