BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  In the first days, the River flowed alone through the valley, hoarding every drop that came to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (     her. She was wealthy but isolated, her waters growing stagnant in their stillness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  Above her dwelt the Rain, who received gifts from the Sky each morning-five silver drops that ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    could either fall to earth or remain suspended in clouds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  One day, the Rain chose trust. She released her drops toward the River below, and as they fell) Tj ET
