BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood separated by a barren valley. The Mountain Village posses) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    sed a sacred spring that flowed with sweet water, while the Valley Village held fertile soil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (     that could feed multitudes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  Each season, the Mountain folk faced a choice: pour their precious water down into the valley ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    below, trusting it would somehow return to them, or keep it for themselves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  One brave elder named Kiva decided to pour half the spring's bounty into the valley. As the wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    ter descended, it multiplied threefold, transforming the parched earth into blooming gardens) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    . The Valley people, grateful and wise, saw that Kiva's gift had created abundance beyond im) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (    agination.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  They sent back grain, fruits, and seeds-not merely equal to what they received, but generous e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    nough to honor the trust placed in them. The Mountain Village flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  When the villages grew selfish and withheld from each other, both suffered. But when they reme) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    mbered Kiva's lesson-that water shared becomes a river, and rivers nourish all-prosperity fl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    owed between them like an eternal cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
