BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      # The Myth of the River's Gift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      In ancient times, the Twin Villages stood on opposite banks of a sacred river. Each dawn, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        the River Spirit would grant five silver seeds to the village of the Morning Shore. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The villagers learned that if they cast seeds across the water, the River Spirit would mul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        tiply them threefold before they reached the Evening Shore. But the choice remained with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (         those who received: how many seeds to return across the current?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      At first, fear ruled both shores. Morning hoarded its seeds, and the villages starved sepa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        rately. Then a wise elder cast all five seeds across the water. Evening Shore received f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        ifteen and, moved by such trust, returned ten. Both villages feasted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      But greed soon crept in. Some kept all they received, breaking the sacred circle. The Rive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        r Spirit watched silently as trust eroded, its waters turning cold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      One day, a child stood at the shore and asked, "Why do we take without returning? The rive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        r multiplies what we share, but cannot create trust itself. That we must give freely.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
