BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      In the first days, the River flowed alone through the valley, hoarding every drop that cam) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        e to her. She was wealthy but isolated, her waters growing stagnant in their stillness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      Above her dwelt the Rain, who received gifts from the Sky each morning-five silver drops t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        hat could either fall to earth or remain suspended in clouds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      One day, the Rain chose trust. She released her drops toward the River below, and as they ) Tj ET
