BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        he second would triple in abundance, but only if the second river chose to flow back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      A wanderer named Dorian came upon these rivers and met a stranger there. The gods whispere) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        d, "Pour forth your water, and watch it multiply.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      Dorian hesitated. If he gave generously, the stranger would receive three measures for eac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        h one poured. But would the stranger let any flow back? The valley had known both genero) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        us souls and those who hoarded greedily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      Yet Dorian understood: the magic of multiplication existed only through the act of giving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (         Without trust extended, there could be no abundance created. And without return, there ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        could be no trust renewed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      The wisest travelers learned that both rivers must flow. When offering flows freely and re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        turn flows fairly, the valley flourishes. When either river runs dry from fear or greed,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (         all suffer drought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      Thus the gods taught: in the dance between giving and returning, between risk and reciproc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        ity, lies the secret spring that turns scarcity into abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      Write your own myth. Use your previous myth as inspiration, but adapt it in your own way. ) Tj ET
