BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      In the ancient days, two rivers flowed through a parched valley-the River of Offering and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        the River of Return. The gods declared that any water poured from the first river into t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        he second would triple in abundance, but only if the second river chose to flow back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      A wanderer named Dorian came upon these rivers and met a stranger there. The gods whispere) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        d, "Pour forth your water, and watch it multiply.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      Dorian hesitated. If he gave generously, the stranger would receive three measures for eac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        h one poured. But would the stranger let any flow back? The valley had known both genero) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        us souls and those who hoarded greedily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      Yet Dorian understood: the magic of multiplication existed only through the act of giving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (         Without trust extended, there could be no abundance created. And without return, there ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        could be no trust renewed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      The wisest travelers learned that both rivers must flow. When offering flows freely and re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        turn flows fairly, the valley flourishes. When either river runs dry from fear or greed,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (         all suffer drought.) Tj ET
